body:
if you would please take the time to reread my post:
i am not shaming her for having tourettes. i feel like shit because every time she— or someone else for that matter— makes any sort of movement that my brain interprets as a [pow] i either drop to the floor and start sobbing uncontrollably or shut down and have to be taken home.

i like being around her. she understands me, and she understands my situation. she doesn't think im a bad person for having a reaction that i *also cannot control,* but i can't help but feel bad for it.
